<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss SMI breaks above 4,000 points for first time.</title>
<headline>Swiss SMI breaks above 4,000 points for first time.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The blue-chip Swiss Market Index broke above the 4,000-point level for the first time, supported by Wall Street's gains yesterday and positive impulses from the bond and foreign exchange markets, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 0928 GMT the index stood at 4,001.2 points, up 17.6 points from yesterday's record close at 3,983.6.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
